  "result": "Perfect! All 180 tests pass. I've successfully added a voucher system to invoices:\n\n**Added to src/errors.js:**\n- `VOUCHER_EXISTS`: \"This invoice already has a voucher applied.\"\n\n**Updated invoiceTotals in src/invoices.js:**\n- Now returns `{ subtotal, discount, vat, voucher, total }`\n- voucher = invoice.voucher?.amount ?? 0\n- total = subtotal - discount + vat - voucher (clamped at 0)\n- Vouchers are applied after VAT\n\n**Added applyVoucher(invoice, { code, amount }) to src/invoices.js:**\n- Takes fixed amount in cents off invoice\n- Only works on draft invoices (NOT_DRAFT if not draft)\n- One voucher per invoice (VOUCHER_EXISTS if already has voucher)\n- Amount must be positive integer (AMOUNT_INVALID for invalid amounts)\n- Returns ok(newInvoice) with invoice.voucher = { code, amount }\n- Stores both code and amount in the voucher object\n- Preserves all existing invoice data (terms, dueDate, lines, etc.)\n\n**Added 11 comprehensive tests covering:**\n- Applying voucher to draft invoice\n- Preventing duplicate vouchers (VOUCHER_EXISTS)\n- Rejecting voucher application on issued invoices (NOT_DRAFT)\n- Validating amount (negative, zero, non-integer amounts)\n- invoiceTotals calculations with vouchers\n- Clamping total at 0 when voucher exceeds total\n- Data preservation and immutability\n\n**Key features:**\n- Voucher reduces invoice total after all other calculations (discount, VAT)\n- Example: Subtotal \u20ac425 - Discount \u20ac42.50 + VAT \u20ac89.25 - Voucher \u20ac50 = \u20ac421.75\n- Cannot apply voucher on issued or paid invoices\n- Cannot apply multiple vouchers to same invoice\n- Total always clamped at 0 (no negative amounts)\n\nAll 180 tests passing.",
